<title>JAPAN: Tokyo Grain Exchange to launch corn option in Sept.</title>
<headline>Tokyo Grain Exchange to launch corn option in Sept.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Tokyo Grain Exchange (TGE) said on Tuesday it will launch options on its corn futures contracts from September 16, in an attempt to provide the local grain industry with a risk hedging tool.</p>
<p>The yen-based corn options contract will be traded on the TGE's automated trading system, an exchange spokesman said.</p>
<p>This will be the third option contract on the TGE, following soybean and raw sugar.</p>
<p>Surging turnover in the TGE corn futures market last year prompted the Japanese exchange to consider launching corn options, the spokesman said.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Comodities Desk (+81-3-3432-7391)</p>
